\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{One pair fixes the source sign}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{Take #{V=\mathbb C} with its standard basis and let #{K=kI}. The [intrinsic paired coefficients and sources](fdip-00IS) have #{\theta=\psi\bar\psi}, #{\Omega_V=\psi\bar\psi}, and
##{e^{-k\bar\psi\psi}=1+k\psi\bar\psi.}
Put #{A=\bar\eta\psi} and #{B=\bar\psi\eta}. These even elements commute and square to zero. Moving the source coefficients left gives #{AB=\bar\eta\eta\psi\bar\psi}. Thus
##{\mathscr Z_k=k+\bar\eta\eta,\qquad
J_V(\psi\bar\psi e^{-k\bar\psi\psi})=1,\qquad
J_V(\bar\psi\psi e^{-k\bar\psi\psi})=-1.}
For #{k\ne0}, this is #{k\exp(\bar\eta k^{-1}\eta)}. The positive sign of the source contraction and the negative sign of the reversed insertion follow from the same paired order.}
